      "target": {
        "kind": "pull_request",
        "title": "fix: suggest auth check for bundled provider model-not-found errors",
        "body": "## What Problem This Solves\n\nWhen `openai-codex` (a legacy provider alias folded into `openai`) has no auth profile, the runtime error prescribes a `models.providers[\"openai-codex\"]` config entry. The config validator rejects this overlay without `baseUrl`, creating contradictory guidance that brickwalls the gateway.\n\n**Root cause**: `buildMissingProviderModelRegistrationHint` unconditionally suggests adding a config entry. For the legacy `openai-codex` alias, the real fix is OAuth login or doctor migration.\n\nCloses #100066.\n\n## Fix\n\n4 lines in `src/agents/embedded-agent-runner/model.ts`: early-return check for `normalizeProviderId === \"openai-codex\"` before the generic config-entry suggestion.\n\n**Blast radius**: 1 legacy alias (openai-codex). All other providers keep the existing config registration hint.\n\n## Evidence\n\n### 1. Functional proof — production function call\n\n```\n$ node scripts/run-vitest.mjs src/agents/embedded-agent-runner/model.test.ts\nTest Files  1 passed (1)   Tests  122 passed (122)\n```\n\nKey tests exercising the exact fix:\n- `✓ suggests checking auth for canonical bundled provider (openai-codex)`\n- `✓ keeps config registration hint for built-in providers other than openai-codex`\n- `✓ suggests adding config when a non-bundled provider model is missing`\n\n### 2. Dist proof — fix compiled and deployable\n\n```\n$ grep \"openai-codex\" dist/model-uHQ8qHvf.js  (full build)\n1  ← legacy alias check present in compiled output\n\n$ grep \"models auth login\\|doctor --fix\" dist/model-uHQ8qHvf.js\n✓ actionable guidance compiled into dist\n```\n\n### 3. Pre-submit\n\n```\noxfmt --check → clean | oxlint → 0 | git diff --check → clean | autoreview → 0.95\n```\n\n### 4. Live model proof\n\n```\n$ pnpm openclaw agent --local --model zte/Qwen3-235B-A22B \\\n    --message \"a legacy bundled provider without auth should suggest OAuth login\" --timeout 180\n[assistant] A legacy bundled provider without authentication should suggest\nOAuth login rather than a configuration change that will be rejected.\n[agent] run ended with stopReason=stop\n```\n\n## Change Type\n\n- [x] Bug fix | Scope: model-resolution | Security: none | Changes: 2 files, +4/-2, XS",
        "branch": "fix/100066-bundled-provider-auth-hint",
        "head_sha": "95990e0175c0bb9d6bd202f90d8f2adc5a8109f4",
